'''''Rinconraptor''''' ({{lit|[[Rincón de Los Sauces|Rincón]] thief}})  is an [[extinct]] genus of [[megaraptorid]] theropod dinosaur known from the [[Late Cretaceous]] ([[Santonian]] age) [[Bajo de la Carpa Formation]] of Argentina. The genus contains a [[Monotypic taxon|single species]], '''''Rinconraptor pipoae''''', known from a partial postcranial skeleton.<ref name="Rinconraptor" />

== Paleoenvironment ==
The remains of ''Rinconraptor'' were recovered from the Bajo de la Carpa Formation, characterized by dominantly [[sandstone]] and muddy [[Shale|sediments]], representing Santonian-aged [[River|fluvial]] and [[Aeolian processes|aeolian]] systems. This formation indicates a semi-arid paleoenvironment that supported a rich terrestrial ecosystem including [[turtle]]s, [[Peirosauridae|peirosaurid]] [[Crocodyliformes|crocodyliform]]s, [[Ornithopoda|ornithopod]]s, [[Abelisauridae|abelisaurid]]s, and [[megaraptora]]ns.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Garrido |first=Alberto C. |date=2010 |title=Estratigrafía del Grupo Neuquén, Cretácico Superior de la Cuenca Neuquina (Argentina): nueva propuesta de ordenamiento litoestratigráfico |url=https://www.scielo.org.ar/scielo.php?script=sci_abstract&pid=S1853-04002010000200003&lng=es&nrm=iso&tlng=es |journal=Revista del Museo Argentino de Ciencias Naturales |language=es |publisher=Museo Argentino de Ciencias Naturales "Bernardino Rivadavia" |volume=12 |issue=2 |pages=121–177 |issn=1853-0400}}</ref>

